      "side": 1,
      "message": "This `justify-content: center` has no effect: `.mobileTitleWrapper .bigTitle` below is `flex: 1 1 0; width: 100%`, so the anchor always fills the wrapper and the title ends up left-aligned next to the hamburger. The commit message says that\u0027s intended, but it changes the look for every host with a short title (previously centered between the 100px gutters).\n\nIf you want to keep short titles centered *and* let long titles use all available space, this does both:\n\n```css\n.mobileTitleWrapper .bigTitle {\n  flex: 0 1 auto; /* shrink-to-fit when short -\u003e centered by wrapper; shrinks -\u003e ellipsis when long */\n  min-width: 0;\n  max-width: 100%;\n}\n```\n\nIf left-aligned is the goal, please drop `justify-content: center` here so the intent is unambiguous.",
